        "original_id": "66969b00-31d3-5a2d-9496-3a568fd53b5a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Leigh Silverman, Jeanine Tesori, Brian Crawley, Doris Betts, David Henry Hwang, Jeff Locker\n- Works: Violet, From Up Here, Chinglish, The Ugliest Pilgrim\n- Roles: stage director, actor\n- Awards: Tony Award, Drama Desk Award\n\nFacts:\n- Leigh Silverman is an American stage director who has worked both Off-Broadway and on Broadway.\n- Leigh Silverman was nominated for the 2008 Drama Desk Award for Outstanding Director of a Play for From Up Here.\n- Chinglish is a comedy about an American businessman who is desperate to launch a new enterprise in China.\n- Jeff Locker starred as Peter Timms in Chinglish by David Henry Hwang.\n- Chinglish opened on Broadway in 2011 with direction by Leigh Silverman.\n- Violet is a musical with music by Jeanine Tesori and a libretto by Brian Crawley.\n- Violet is based on the short story The Ugliest Pilgrim by Doris Betts.\n- Leigh Silverman was nominated for the 2014 Tony Award for Best Direction of a Musical for Violet.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
