        "original_id": "9be5397f-bba4-5e1f-b65e-3cb573d0d39c",
        "text": "Page: Leigh Silverman. Sentence: Leigh Silverman is an American director for the stage, both Off-Broadway and on Broadway.\nPage: Leigh Silverman. Sentence: She was nominated for the 2014 Tony Award, Best Direction of a Musical for the musical \"Violet\" and the 2008 Drama Desk Award, Outstanding Director of a Play for the play \"From Up Here\".\nPage: Violet (musical). Sentence: Violet is a musical with music by Jeanine Tesori and libretto by Brian Crawley based on the short story \"The Ugliest Pilgrim\" by Doris Betts.\nPage: Chinglish (play). Sentence: It is a comedy about an American businessman desperate to launch a new enterprise in China, which opened on Broadway in 2011 with direction by Leigh Silverman.\nPage: Jeff Locker. Sentence: \", and starred as Peter Timms in the play \"Chinglish\" by David Henry Hwang.",
